    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.48,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.85,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings are flat at about 1.34 from 7 h to 18 h, which looks like a plateau. I diluted the 18 h aliquot and scaled the readings back up. These were the results:\n- 10x dilution: 0.1467 mean, which scales to about 1.47.\n- 20x dilution: 0.0737 mean, which scales to about 1.47.\n- 50x dilution: 0.0308 mean, which scales to about 1.54. This one is noisier because the signal is so low.\n\nAll three dilutions agree with each other at about 1.47–1.54. That is consistently higher than the undiluted reading of about 1.34, so the undiluted reading is compressed at high OD. The plateau therefore understates the late biomass by roughly 10%. The size of the gap is modest, which is why I put the probability at 0.85 and not higher."
